derstand that he was now removed from consideration as a human being.","ref":"1913, Norman Lindsay, A Curate in Bohemia, Sydney: N.S.W. Bookstall Co., published 1932, page 141:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[92,95]],"id":"5339f502-cc82-406e-b551-290bb9e9b834"},{"text":"“Bah!” cried the woman. “My husband will know!”","ref":"1913 June–December, Edgar Rice Burroughs, “Forging Bonds of Hate and ——?”, in The Return of Tarzan, New York, N.Y.: A[lbert] L[evi] Burt Company, […], published March 1915, →OCLC, page 22:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[1,4]],"id":"7ed5d2a2-6253-47ea-b786-c81d3000d9d1"},{"text":"Templeton looked over the assembled servants speculatively, then shrugged. \"Bah!\" he said. \"They're of no use to me. Come, Andrew, a word with you upstairs.\"","ref":"1992, April Kihlstrom, Dangerous Masquerade:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[76,79]],"id":"faf37154-a3d2-4a03-a93d-2838972573f0"}],"categories":["English humorous terms","English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(sometimes humorous) Expressing contempt, disgust, or bad temper."],"glosses":["Expressing contempt, disgust, or bad temper."],"tags":["humorous","sometimes"],"id":"8f48e04c-41b9-4daa-8fdd-421d11bfbe78"}],"related":[{"word":"contempt","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"despise","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"sneer","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"tut tut","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"yuck","source":"Thesaurus:bah"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"expressing contempt","word":"pht"},{"word":"feh"},{"word":"meh"},{"word":"pooh"},{"word":"pshaw"},{"word":"poh"},{"word":"pish"},{"sense":"expressing disgust","word":"bleh"},{"word":"ick"},{"word":"ych a fi"},{"word":"yuck"},{"word":"bah","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"blech","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"bleck","source":"Thesaurus:bah","tags":["rare"]},{"word":"faugh","source":"Thesaurus:bah","tags":["dated"]},{"word":"faw","source":"Thesaurus:bah"},{"word":"foh","source":"Thesaurus:bah","tags":["obsole